  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration found is config_010 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.7250). All other tested variants with the same encoders but different aggregation/fusion (config_050: transformer+concat=0.7207, config_041: avgpool+weighted=0.7062) show consistent degradation. The only untested configuration retaining both top encoders (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l) is config_016 (avgpool + concat). Question: This tests whether the avgpool+concat combination with the best encoders could unexpectedly match or exceed the transformer+weighted result, closing the last gap in the scvi_n200+ViT-L subgrid. Rationale: As the final experiment, this is the highest-ceiling untested option given that all other untested configs substitute a weaker RNA encoder (pca_n2000, scgpt) or image encoder (resnet50), both of which have shown substantial performance drops (0.52–0.59 range). While config_016 is unlikely to surpass 0.7250, it is the most informative remaining test and confirms the design-space boundary. Expected cost: ~4.5–5.0 GPU hours (similar to config_041 at 4.82 h, since avgpool+concat vs avgpool+weighted is a minor fusion change), bringing total to ~43 GPU hours."
}

